    rationale: `DSM-5-TR notes that recurrent vomiting can cause significant, permanent loss of dental enamel and enlarged salivary glands, especially the parotid glands. People who induce vomiting by triggering the gag reflex with a hand may develop calluses or scars on its back. A counselor who notices such signs raises concerns gently and arranges medical evaluation, since purging can cause dangerous electrolyte imbalances.`,
    references: [{ source: 'DSM-5-TR', detail: 'Bulimia nervosa: associated features (dental enamel loss, parotid enlargement, calluses on the hand)' }],
